# Performance and packaging

Runtime packages must stay **tree-shakeable** and **side-effect free on import** so consumers pay only for subpaths they import.

## Exports map

- **Identical subpaths** after `@rosettadash/<runtime>/` on all five packages (manifest-driven).
- Each subpath entry: `{ types, import, default }` minimum.
- Svelte adds `"svelte"` condition pointing at `.svelte` source.
- WC adds CSS entries: `./tokens.css`, `./styles.css`, `./browser/media`.

Do not add root-only barrel re-exports that pull entire library — prefer subpath imports.

## Side effects

- Avoid module-level registration, DOM mutation, or global listeners on import.
- If a file must register CEs, do so lazily on first use.
- Set `"sideEffects": false` in package.json unless CSS/assets require exception (list explicit paths).

## Dependencies vs peerDependencies

| Kind | Declare as |
|------|------------|
| `@rosettadash/core` | dependency (shared types/math) |
| `three`, map libs, `@ffmpeg/*` | **peerDependency** + dynamic import at runtime |
| Framework (react, vue, …) | peerDependency |
| Tailwind, MUI, CSS Modules | **never** in runtime packages |

Document third-party peer installs in package README and export `README.export.md` — not RosettaDash runtime deps in standalone export mode.

## Tree-shaking patterns

- Named exports only on subpaths — no default-export entire library from deep paths.
- Split heavy optional code (Three scene, ffmpeg worker) into separate subpaths or lazy chunks.
- `@rosettadash/web-components/browser/media` — pre-bundled ESM for no-build consumers; do not duplicate ffmpeg in each framework package.

## Object URLs and memory

- Revoke `URL.createObjectURL` in cleanup/disconnect.
- Dispose Three.js geometries/materials/textures in `disconnectedCallback` / unmount.
- Cancel `requestAnimationFrame` and `IntersectionObserver` on teardown.

## Build and pack

| Script | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `npm run pack:consumer` | Build core + all runtimes + browser/media bundle + pack tgz |
| `nx build web-components` | TSC multi-entry + `bundle-browser-media.mjs` |

Verify pack output: importing one subpath must not require downloading unrelated atoms.

## Size discipline

- Prefer CSS + tokens over JS for static visuals (bar chart fallback heights, skeleton shimmer via CSS).
- Do not ship duplicate Three.js helpers across WC/React/Angular — shared logic in core or WC, frameworks wrap.

## Checklist

- [ ] New subpath added to all runtime `package.json` exports (via codegen)
- [ ] No new module-scope side effects
- [ ] Heavy libs peer + lazy loaded
- [ ] Cleanup on unmount documented in component

